=== systemd-analyze verify — post-install, session 020 ===

Cmd:  systemd-analyze verify /usr/lib/systemd/system/tbard.service
Target: the installed unit at /usr/lib/systemd/system/tbard.service
        (NOT the in-repo packaging/systemd/tbard.service copy)

Output (verbatim, complete):
  (no output on stdout, no output on stderr)
  EXIT=0

Contrast with the PRE-INSTALL evidence (docs/test-logs/015/systemd-analyze-verify.log
and the v0.2.0 bench pack): pre-install, with /usr/bin/tbard absent,
`systemd-analyze verify` emitted:
  tbard.service: Failed to create tbard.service/start: Unit file …
  … has no ExecStart=, which is not allowed: one of the lines below failed to parse
  /usr/bin/tbard: No such file or directory            (exit 1)
The unit structurally parsed, but verify exited 1 because the ExecStart
target did not exist on disk. Now that the binary is installed at
/usr/bin/tbard (sha256 d1279e1f…, see install-evidence.log §1),
`systemd-analyze verify` exits 0 with no diagnostics. The pre-install
exit-1 evidence is closed.

NOTE: this verifies the unit's STATIC correctness (syntax + ExecStart
path exists + dependencies resolvable). It does NOT validate runtime
behaviour, hardening correctness under privdrop, or the ADR-019/033
restart-rate-limit math. Those remain Stage-3 acceptance items.